> This Technical Services Advisory Agreement ('Agreement') is made and\
> entered into as of \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_2024 (the\
> 'Effective Date') by and between Advanced Energy Technologies\
> Proprietary Limited (hereinafter 'AET') a private, limited liability\
> company registered in South Africa with Company Registration Number\
> 2024/171062/07 and with its principle place of business located at 660\
> Willowgrove Road, Dainfern, 2191, Johannesburg, South Africa, and\
> Waltkon Energy Proprietary Limited (in formation) (hereinafter\
> 'Waltkon Energy'), a private, limited liability company registered in\
> South Africa with Company Registration Number\
> \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_/\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_/\\_\\_ and with its principle place of\
> business located at \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
> \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_,\
> \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, South Africa.\
>\
> In this Agreement, Advanced Energy Technologies Proprietary Limited\
> (hereinafter AET, alternatively 'Advisor') and Waltkon Energy\
> Proprietary Limited (hereinafter Waltkon Energy) each may be\
> individually referred to as a 'Signatory Party', and collectively, as\
> the 'Signatory Parties'.\
>\
> This Agreement replaces and cancels any previous agreements in writing\
> or otherwise between the Signatory Parties, and in consideration of\
> the mutual promises and agreements herein contained and other good and\
> valuable considerations, the receipt and sufficiency of which is\
> hereby acknowledged, and accepted, it is hereby agreed between the\
> Signatory parties hereto as follows:\
>\
> **\\\
> **\
>\
> **1. ADVISORY SERVICES**\
\
1.  The Advisor undertakes to act as a non-exclusive Advisor to Waltkon\
    > Energy, and shall, provide technical and project advisory services\
    > to Waltkon Energy as further described in \'a72 hereto, including,\
    > but not be limited to, reviewing, and analyzing any material\
    > documentation provided by Waltkon Energy to the Advisor and\
    > interfacing, collaborating and advising potential suppliers,\
    > Engineering Procurement and Construction Management (EPC) firms,\
    > equipment suppliers and/or any third-party engineering firms, that\
    > the Advisor believes Waltkon Energy may benefit from.\
\
2.  Consistent with its duties described in 1.1 above, the Advisor shall\
    > use its best efforts to provide technical and project advice to\
    > Waltkon Energy. If Waltkon Energy requests the Advisor to perform\
    > any other specific services, such services shall be described in\
    > an addendum hereto, and in a form to be agreed upon by both\
    > Signatory Parties.\
\
3.  Consistent with its duties described herein, the Advisor shall\
    > maintain absolute confidentiality with respect to these services\
    > and shall not provide any verbal or written information to any\
    > external party without the express written permission of Waltkon\
    > Energy.\
\
> **2. ADVISORY SERVICES**\
>\
> Advisor will provide the following advice and recommendations to\
> Waltkon Energy, and, upon Waltkon Energy's direction, such information\
> shall be supplied and disseminated to the companies, suppliers,\
> vendors, and sub-contractors selected and under management of and duly\
> appointed by Waltkon Energy, EPC(M) Contractor as a basis for its\
> submissions and recommendations to Waltkon Energy for its final\
> approval of such engineering and construction recommendations and the\
> associated terms and pricing thereto for the balance-of-plant\
> implementation.\
>\
> 2.1. Advisor will collaborate, with input from Waltkon Energy and\
> EPC(M), to determine the overall scope and indicative design of the\
> plant, necessary to meet marketable product outputs objectives of the\
> Naboomspruit Renewable Fuels Production Facility.\
>\
> 2.2. Advisor will determine and recommend the number of A-2800 A-T-E-C\
> Reformer units necessary to meet Waltkon Energy's initial and\
> subsequent expansion consideration of the Naboomspruit Renewable Fuels\
> production objectives.\
>\
> 2.3. Advisor will provide technical specifications on all A-2800\
> A-T-E-C Reformer liquid / gaseous outputs and will further identify\
> the multiple processes necessary to convert such outputs into\
> marketable products.\
>\
> 2.4. Advisor will recommend gas / liquids output management equipment\
> and processes for separation, consumption, and release, specifically\
> for recommended compliance in plant permitting.\
>\
> (South African SANS 1598 and SANS 342 are Compliance Standards which\
> outline the allowable limits and criteria for various physical and\
> chemical parameters for liquid fuels, including density, octane\
> number, sulfur content, and benzene content are the applicable\
> standards\\].\
>\
> 2.5. Advisor will produce process flow diagram (PFD) with mass balance\
> as preliminary working documentation.\
>\
> 2.6. Advisor will produce preliminary working document for the piping\
> and instrumentation diagram (P&ID). This will include recommended\
> interconnect systems, such as DCS or some other integrated control\
> system.\
>\
> 2.7. Advisor will produce a working document providing a general scope\
> single-line electrical diagram, which will include estimated power\
> consumption including HP based on an indicative plant design.\
>\
> 2.8. Advisor will produce a CAD drawing indicating feedstock stockyard\
> handling and A-2800 A-TEC Reformer input delivery systems for\
> reference by the selected EPC(M).\
>\
> 2.9. Advisor will produce a generalized process water system\
> determination by heat and mass balance. (Heaters, water tower, and\
> discharge water treatment). This will be an initial general plan to\
> begin meeting compliance with the water waste discharge requirements\
> under the South African National Water Act, (Act 36 of 1998 (as\
> amended)). A specific approach for this process must be supplied by\
> Company's selected EPC(M).\
>\
> 2.10. Advisor will produce a major component plant equipment list, to\
> include A-2800 A-TEC Reformer units, distillation column(s), tankage,\
> (pre-hydrotreat, post-hydrotreat, gases, load-out), plant air\
> compressor capacity, and further materials handling equipment such as\
> conveyor belts, tractors, forklifts, and other mechanized vehicles\
> necessary to efficiently operate the facility contemplated herein.\
>\
> 2.11. Advisor will provide advice and recommendations regarding the\
> indicative financial modeling for the capital expenditure /\
> operational expenditure, including recommended personnel headcounts\
> for operations and maintenance, based on the indicative design\
> parameters produced by Advisor and EPC(M) for Waltkon Energy.\
>\
> 2.12. Advisor will recommend an indicative site plan including\
> calculations for traffic flow analysis, plant layout indicating\
> structure layouts, average truck and heavy equipment operation for air\
> permitting (South African compliance standard under the Air Quality\
> Act No. 39 of 2004 (as amended) for Company's selected plant site. A\
> specific approach for this process must be supplied by Company's\
> selected EPC(M).\
>\
> Advisor will make every reasonable attempt in collaboration with the\
> EPC(M) at confirming static pricing and product availability for the\
> procurement, logistics and commissioning costs. It must be noted that\
> prices and availability may change seasonally and with prevailing\
> demand-and-supply circumstances, and therefore, it is specifically\
> recorded and hereby stated that all Priced Proposals and/or Quotation\
> are provided on an indicative basis and should not be construed as\
> final price-firm quotations, unless it is specifically so-stated in\
> the relevant documentation provided by all vendors in this regard.\
>\
> Advisor's Services as described hereunder are for the provision of\
> PRELIMINARY PRE-ENGINEERING DOCUMENTATION ONLY and do not constitute\
> final engineering specification(s) or executable / buildable plan(s).\
> It is the responsibility of Waltkon Energy to engage a qualified\
> EPC(M) contractor, and only to use the documents provided in terms\
> hereof as a basis to determine the final executable scope, plant\
> design, and costing documentation.\
>\
> **3. FEE FOR TECHNICAL ADVISORY SERVICES**\
>\
> 3.1 For services to be rendered hereunder, Waltkon Energy will pay to\
> the Advisor a non-refundable Advisory Fee for services in the amount\
> of two million, five hundred thousand United States Dollars (US\\$\
> 2,500,000.^00^) in advance of any work commencement.\
>\
> This Advisory Fee shall be exclusively for the services identified in\
> \'a72. hereof.\
>\
> If any additional services are requested by Waltkon Energy not\
> specifically identified in \'a72. hereof, additional compensation may be\
> required by the Advisor to perform such services. Under such\
> circumstances, Waltkon Energy and Advisor will execute an addendum\
> attached hereto duly specifying the additional services to be\
> performed and the agreed compensation for such services requested by\
> Waltkon Energy. Advisor at its sole discretion may refuse Waltkon\
> Energy's request and elect not to perform such services, without any\
> further obligation to Waltkon Energy. Any additional services agreed\
> to and provided by the Advisor and documented in an Addendum hereto\
> shall comply with and become an integral part of this Agreement.\
>\
> **4. EXPENSES**\
>\
> 4.1 Advisor and Company agree that Waltkon Energy will pay for or\
> reimburse the Advisor for only those expenses that are agreed upon in\
> advance in writing.\
>\
> 4.2 The Advisor hereby acknowledges that if no agreement with Waltkon\
> Energy regarding reimbursement of certain expenses is made prior to\
> any such expenses being incurred, then Waltkon Energy shall have no\
> obligation to reimburse Advisor for any such expenses.\
>\
> **5. SERVICES TO OTHER COMPANIES**\
>\
> 5.1 The services of the Advisor hereunder are not exclusive.\
>\
> 5.2 The Advisor is free to render services to others and engage in\
> other activities, provided, however, that such other services and\
> activities do not, during the term of this Agreement, interfere with\
> Advisor's services as specified in \'a72. hereof.\
>\
> **6. CONFIDENTIALITY**\
>\
> 6.1 The Advisor and Waltkon Energy shall be bound by a separate Mutual\
> Non-Disclosure Agreement which is separate and distinct from this\
> Agreement.\
>\
> **7. STANDARD OF CARE**\
>\
> 7.1 In the absence of willful misfeasance, bad faith, gross negligence\
> or reckless disregard of obligations or duties hereunder on the part\
> of the Advisor, the Advisor shall not be subject to liability to\
> Waltkon Energy or to any director shareholder, employee, or agent\
> thereof for any act or omission in the course of, or connected with,\
> rendering services hereunder.\
>\
> **8. TERM OF AGREEMENT; AMENDMENTS**\
>\
> 8.1 This Agreement shall commence as of the date hereof and, subject\
> to prior termination as provided in \'a77, clause 8.2 hereof, and shall\
> continue in force until \\_\\_\\_, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ 2024.\
>\
> 8.3 This Agreement may be modified only by the mutual written consent\
> of Waltkon Energy and Advisor.\
>\
> **9. ADVISOR BEST EFFORTS; COMPANY INDEMNITY**\
>\
> 9.1 Advisor shall employ it's best efforts in the performance of the\
> technical and project advisory services to be performed hereunder.\
>\
> 9.2 All recommendations and instructions made by the Advisor will be\
> based upon information received from Waltkon Energy and from sources\
> that it believes to be reliable, but whose accuracy is not and cannot\
> be guaranteed. Such information may or may not have been independently\
> verified by the Advisor.\
>\
> 9.3 Waltkon Energy agrees to indemnify Advisor and hold it harmless\
> from and against any liability of any nature resulting from Waltkon\
> Energy furnishing information provided and approved by Waltkon Energy\
> that is false or inaccurate.\
>\
> **10. NOTICES**\
>\
> 10.1 Except as otherwise specifically provided herein, all notices or\
> communications provided for herein shall be in writing and delivered\
> in person, by overnight mail, by dated electronic mail or by facsimile\
> followed by a hard copy sent first-class mail postage prepaid, and\
> addressed as follows, or to such other address or addresses as may be\
> designated by either Signatory Party by written notice to the other.\
>\
> **11. GOVERNING LAW; ARBITRATION**\
>\
> 11.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance\
> with the laws of the Republic of South Africa.\
>\
> 11.2 All disputes between the Signatory Parties arising out of or\
> relating to the Agreement shall be submitted to and settled by\
> arbitration as hereinafter provided:\
>\
> 11.2.1 Arbitration proceedings shall be governed by a panel of three\
> (3) arbitrators experienced in the matters at hand.\
>\
> 11.2.2 Each Signatory Party shall select one arbitrator, and the third\
> arbitrator shall be selected upon mutual agreement of the first two\
> arbitrators, in accordance with the Commercial Arbitration Rules of\
> the Arbitration Foundation of Southern Africa (AFSA).\
>\
> 11.2.3 The arbitration proceeding shall be held in Johannesburg, South\
> Africa, at a location agreed to by the Signatory Parties involved and\
> AFSA.\
>\
> **12. ILLEGALITY; UNENFORCEABILITY**\
>\
> If any provision of this Agreement is found to be illegal or\
> unenforceable, all other provisions to the Agreement shall remain in\
> full force and effect, and both Signatory Parties hereby agree that\
> the intent of the Agreement and any Addenda will take precedent over\
> the text of the document. \uc0\u8195 \
>\
